      <memberdef kind="function" id="classiceberg_1_1LocationUtil_1afe4d1878a2457b0ce17fae310146fd1e" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>static std::string iceberg::LocationUtil::ResolveLocation</definition>
        <argsstring>(std::string_view table_location, std::string_view location)</argsstring>
        <name>ResolveLocation</name>
        <qualifiedname>iceberg::LocationUtil::ResolveLocation</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>std::string_view</type>
          <declname>table_location</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>std::string_view</type>
          <declname>location</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Resolve a location against a table location. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A location with a URI scheme is absolute and is returned unchanged. Otherwise the result is <computeroutput>table_location + &quot;/&quot; + location</computeroutput>, with no <computeroutput>/</computeroutput> added when the table location already ends in one. The join does not interpret <computeroutput>.</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>..</computeroutput>, and a location starting with <computeroutput>/</computeroutput> yields <computeroutput>//</computeroutput>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
